{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on dfc980c5: O3's client-metadata fetch policy.\n\nAccepted as proposed. dap fetches a client ID metadata document only\nfrom an exact HTTPS origin in a deployment list. The default list is\nhttps://claude.ai and https://chatgpt.com, and an operator can add\nothers explicitly. Name the setting OAUTH_CLIENT_METADATA_ORIGINS, and\ntreat an invalid setting as closing the OAuth routes, as the other MCP\nsettings do.\n\nKeep every bound you named: an unknown origin refuses before any\nfetch; no credentials; no redirects; at most 5 KiB; a 5-second\ntimeout; exact client_id equality; a cache of at most one hour. The\nconsent page shows the client ID's host beside any name the document\ngives.\n\nThis policy trusts the listed origins and their DNS. It does not\nverify the socket address, and the note must say so in one sentence.\nNo arbitrary-origin fetch and no new egress adapter belong to O3. If a\nlater host needs an origin outside the list, the operator adds it, or\nthe client uses dynamic registration under the redirect policy.\n\nAdd one item to the design's record: the CIMD draft cited is\ndraft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document-02, work in progress.\n\nThis request carries a landing target, so it closes when O3 lands.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}